# Trivy Ignore Configuration for Serverless Blog Infrastructure
# Requirements: 12.2, 12.5
#
# This file defines exceptions for Trivy security scanning.
# Keep synchronized with .checkov.yaml skip rules.
#
# Format: AVD-AWS-XXXX or avd-aws-XXXX
# See: https://avd.aquasec.com/ for rule details
#
# Phase 2: Local Defense (Trivy pre-commit)
# - Block HIGH/CRITICAL severity issues locally
# - Allow documented exceptions for business/architecture reasons

# ======================================
# S3 Bucket Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0089: S3 bucket has logging disabled
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_18 - CloudTrail provides audit trail.
# Terraform state bucket cannot log to itself.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0089

# AVD-AWS-0090: S3 bucket does not have versioning enabled
# Note: NOT ignored - versioning IS enabled on all buckets

# AVD-AWS-0132: S3 bucket does not encrypt data with customer managed key
# Justification: AWS-managed keys (AES256) sufficient for blog content.
# CMK adds cost and complexity without significant security benefit for non-PII data.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0132

# ======================================
# DynamoDB Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0024: DynamoDB table point-in-time recovery not enabled
# Note: NOT ignored - PITR IS enabled on DynamoDB table

# AVD-AWS-0025: DynamoDB table uses AWS managed encryption
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_119 - AWS-managed keys sufficient
# for non-PII blog post data.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0025

# ======================================
# Lambda Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0066: Lambda functions should have X-Ray tracing enabled (LOW)
# Justification: X-Ray is Active only in prd (enable_xray); dev uses PassThrough
# to reduce cost. The Lambda@Edge public-404 function cannot use X-Ray at all
# (inline CKV_AWS_50 skip in modules/cdn/public404.tf).
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0066

# AVD-AWS-0067: Lambda function permission has no source ARN (CRITICAL)
# Note: NOT ignored - every aws_lambda_permission sets source_arn.
# Never ignore this check globally.

# Trivy has no check for Lambda DLQs (CKV_AWS_116) or Lambda environment
# variable encryption (CKV_AWS_173); those Checkov skips have no Trivy counterpart.

# ======================================
# API Gateway Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0001: API Gateway access logging not enabled
# Note: This should NOT be ignored for production.
# Implemented in modules/api/main.tf (aws_cloudwatch_log_group.api_access_logs,
# aws_api_gateway_stage.main access_log_settings), gated on local.is_production
# so it is enabled in prd and disabled in dev to reduce cost and noise.

# AVD-AWS-0004: No unauthorized access to API Gateway methods (LOW)
# Note: NOT ignored - public read endpoints (and CORS OPTIONS methods) are
# intentionally unauthenticated; admin endpoints use COGNITO_USER_POOLS.

# AVD-AWS-0005: API Gateway domain name uses outdated SSL/TLS protocols (HIGH)
# Note: NOT ignored - no API Gateway custom domain is defined; the API is
# reached through CloudFront (see AVD-AWS-0013).

# AVD-AWS-0190: API Gateway REST API response caching not enabled (LOW)
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_120 - CloudFront provides edge caching for
# /api/* paths; API Gateway caching would duplicate it and add an hourly charge.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0190

# ======================================
# CloudFront Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0011: CloudFront distribution does not have a WAF in front
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_86 - a regional WAF web ACL adds a monthly base fee
# plus per-rule and per-request charges, which isn't justified for this personal blog.
# There is no CloudFront-level rate limiting (no WAF, no CloudFront rate-based rule);
# the only rate limiting that exists is API Gateway stage/method throttling
# (modules/api: stage-wide 100 rps / burst 200, plus a lower per-method limit on
# admin write methods - 10 rps / burst 20 by default - added in #682). No PII data
# is served or stored by this application.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0011

# AVD-AWS-0010: CloudFront distribution does not have access logging configured (MEDIUM)
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_68 - S3 storage cost.
# CloudWatch metrics provide sufficient visibility.
# Review-by: 2026-10-31 (CloudFront access logging is proposed in #684)
AVD-AWS-0010

# AVD-AWS-0012: CloudFront distribution allows unencrypted (HTTP) communications (CRITICAL)
# Note: NOT ignored - every cache behavior in modules/cdn uses
# viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https". Never ignore this check globally.

# AVD-AWS-0013: CloudFront distribution uses outdated SSL/TLS protocols (HIGH)
# Note: NOT ignored - TLSv1.2_2021 security policy configured (see CKV_AWS_174
# in .checkov.yaml for the dev default-certificate caveat)

# ======================================
# Cognito Rules
# ======================================

# Trivy has no Cognito User Pool MFA check. (AVD-AWS-0022 is DocumentDB
# customer-managed-key encryption, which does not apply here; admin MFA is
# tracked in #677.)

# ======================================
# CloudWatch Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0017: CloudWatch log group not encrypted with CMK
# Justification: Same as CKV_AWS_158 - no PII in logs.
# Default encryption is sufficient.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0017

# ======================================
# SNS Rules
# ======================================

# AVD-AWS-0095: SNS topic does not have encryption enabled
# Justification: Alarm notifications contain non-sensitive operational data.
# CMK encryption adds cost without significant security benefit.
# Review-by: 2027-03-31
AVD-AWS-0095

# ======================================
# General/Terraform Rules
# ======================================

# Note: Trivy does not check module source versioning like Checkov.
# CKV_TF_1/CKV_TF_2 equivalents are not applicable in Trivy.

# ======================================
# Synchronization Note
# ======================================
# This file should be kept in sync with .checkov.yaml
# When adding/removing skip rules:
# 1. Update both .checkov.yaml and .trivyignore
# 2. Document justification in both files
# 3. Run: pre-commit run --all-files (to verify Trivy)
# 4. Run: checkov -d . (to verify Checkov)
